## Phase 9 — Security & Hardening

- [ ] CSRF tokens on all forms
- [ ] Prepared statements everywhere (already using `mysqli` — use `$conn->prepare()`)
- [ ] Input sanitization with `htmlspecialchars()` and `filter_input()`
- [ ] Role-based access guards on every controller action
- [ ] Rate-limit OTP requests
- [ ] File upload validation (type, size, rename)
- [ ] Add `.htaccess` to block direct access to `config/`, `models/`, `errors.log`

> [!CAUTION]
> Never expose `errors.log` or `config/db.php` to the web. Add an `.htaccess` deny rule or move them above the web root.

